{"diagnosis": "Fetch monitor reports TRAP: no progress max_addr=0x00000000 vs expected advance through 256-word NOP mem. set_mem_do_wdata is stuck at 1 at picorv32.v:1408 instead of 0, holding the mem interface in write mode so mem_do_rinst fetches via decoder_trigger/launch_next_insn never complete. This directly blocks progress and matches the fingerprint trap.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -1406,3 +1406,3 @@
 		set_mem_do_rinst = 0;
 		set_mem_do_rdata = 0;
-		set_mem_do_wdata = 1;
+		set_mem_do_wdata = 0;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), max_addr progress >0x00000000, TRAP cleared"}

